On Friday 14 November 2003 19:25 Nudger wrote:

> What are they for? Dumping on alters?

Please don't put half of your question in the subject line and the other
half in the message body; some people don't see both at the same time.
It's civil to use a descriptive subject line and put *all* the
information in the body (even if some of it is in the subject already).

And it's "altars". Alters are separate personalities in the same body,
and they don't tend to take kindly to being dumped on.

That said...

Yes, you can carry a statue on an altar and drop it, but that doesn't do
anything useful except tell you that the statue is uncursed (they
always are, unless your predecessor had one in inventory).

They're made of stone; the stone-to-flesh spell works. Also, breaking
the statue (with a pick-axe, a mattock, a wand of striking or a force
bolt; wands of digging don't work though digging implements do)
produces rocks and *may* reveal an object hidden in the statue. The
deeper in the dungeon the statue was generated (no use carrying them
downstairs) the greater the chance that there's actually an object
inside.

